1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,880
9... 8... 7... 6... 5...!

2
00:00:14,170 --> 00:00:15,960
Defensive foul! 2 free-throws!

3
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:21,950
Yoko! Way to go, Yoko! 
You're my savior right now!

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,710
Please don't start crying!

5
00:00:22,170 --> 00:00:23,920
This game is super close....

6
00:00:23,920 --> 00:00:25,880
Kuzu High is really hanging in there!

7
00:00:26,130 --> 00:00:28,210
Even though they usually always 
lose in the first round.

8
00:00:28,290 --> 00:00:30,250
They're 2 points behind with 4 seconds left.

9
00:00:30,920 --> 00:00:34,460
But they've got 2 free throws coming up,
which means it's possible...

10
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:42,710
She nailed it!

11
00:00:43,170 --> 00:00:44,380
Now it's a 1-point game!

12
00:00:44,830 --> 00:00:46,210
Just one basket away...

13
00:00:46,210 --> 00:00:47,460
It's down to the wire.

14
00:00:47,880 --> 00:00:51,170
Kuzu High isn't very good at getting rebounds,
and a tie would mean overtime.

15
00:00:51,170 --> 00:00:53,420
It's going to be really 
rough for them, either way.

16
00:00:57,130 --> 00:00:59,500
Please... just go in!

17
00:01:00,130 --> 00:01:02,000
Go in! Go in!

18
00:01:04,290 --> 00:01:06,210
Go in! Go in!

19
00:01:07,880 --> 00:01:08,380
She missed!

20
00:01:08,380 --> 00:01:08,920
Rebound!

21
00:01:09,460 --> 00:01:12,460
Uh, it's coming right 
at me...! What do I do?!

22
00:01:16,460 --> 00:01:16,960
What the...?

23
00:01:17,210 --> 00:01:18,380
Sh-she did it...

24
00:01:18,790 --> 00:01:20,830
Surround her! Do everything 
you can to prevent a shot!

25
00:01:21,250 --> 00:01:23,500
Senpai! Save me!

26
00:01:23,580 --> 00:01:24,540
3...!

27
00:01:26,750 --> 00:01:27,710
2...!

28
00:01:28,170 --> 00:01:29,420
1...!

29
00:01:39,630 --> 00:01:40,460
Time's up!

30
00:01:46,080 --> 00:01:48,790
I'm so sorry... it's my fault...

31
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:51,210
I screwed up our last chance!

32
00:01:51,380 --> 00:01:54,540
Me, too... because I missed 
that second free throw!

33
00:01:54,540 --> 00:01:57,330
Right, but that's okay. 
Don't beat yourselves up.

34
00:01:58,380 --> 00:02:01,210
We had a ton of fun playing out there
with you girls to the end.

35
00:02:01,210 --> 00:02:02,210
Thanks a bunch.

36
00:02:06,710 --> 00:02:08,880
Nooo! Please don't quit!

37
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:11,670
Cut it out! You know we have to start studying
for college entrance exams!

38
00:02:13,580 --> 00:02:15,670
Let go of me, you big crybabies!

39
00:02:17,170 --> 00:02:18,500
Don't get all mopey on us.

40
00:02:19,170 --> 00:02:21,210
We're leaving the team in your hands now.
So toughen up...

41
00:02:21,540 --> 00:02:22,630
I really...

42
00:02:28,130 --> 00:02:29,170
I really wanted...

43
00:02:31,130 --> 00:02:32,670
I so wanted us to win this...!

44
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:37,750
There, there.

45
00:02:41,580 --> 00:02:42,630
Senpai...

46
00:03:13,330 --> 00:03:16,040
Ahiru no Sora

47
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:19,880
Let's go, let's go! Shinjo!

48
00:04:19,880 --> 00:04:21,130
Let's go, let's go! Shinjo!

49
00:04:21,170 --> 00:04:22,710
Crush 'em, crush 'em! Shinjo!

50
00:04:22,710 --> 00:04:24,040
Crush 'em, crush 'em! Shinjo!

51
00:04:24,290 --> 00:04:24,830
Rebound!

52
00:04:29,830 --> 00:04:32,250
Shinjo's going for zone defense, eh?

53
00:04:32,750 --> 00:04:35,170
Well, they've got two 190 centimeter giants.

54
00:04:35,830 --> 00:04:38,670
Yeah, not even Kuzu High's 
#11 can slip by them easily.

55
00:04:39,170 --> 00:04:40,290
C'mon!

56
00:04:40,290 --> 00:04:42,670
Oh, looks like they've 
changed up their formation.

57
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:45,420
It's the first time we've seen 
their #7 play in the post.

58
00:04:49,170 --> 00:04:50,290
A spin!

59
00:04:52,790 --> 00:04:53,580
That was smooth.

60
00:04:55,830 --> 00:04:57,210
A return pass?!

61
00:05:07,460 --> 00:05:09,710
Timeout by Shinjotowa Academy!

62
00:05:10,040 --> 00:05:12,300
That was sick! Their #7 has some real skills.

63
00:05:12,300 --> 00:05:13,950
Kuzu High might be tough to beat!

64
00:05:14,500 --> 00:05:16,490
Shinjo's defense is solid, though.

65
00:05:16,490 --> 00:05:19,340
Except that first basket,
Kuzu's only been scoring from mid-range.

66
00:05:19,340 --> 00:05:20,920
This is gonna be a close game for sure.

67
00:05:21,170 --> 00:05:23,130
Nice, nice! We're off to a good start!

68
00:05:23,420 --> 00:05:26,210
I know, right? I've already got them
begging for mercy out there!

69
00:05:26,210 --> 00:05:28,790
As if. You haven't done 
much of anything yet, dude.

70
00:05:29,670 --> 00:05:31,750
Things have gone well and 
put us in a solid position.

71
00:05:32,170 --> 00:05:35,210
We've been quick to switchover to defense,
and there've been no problems so far.

72
00:05:35,830 --> 00:05:37,420
Keep that praise coming!

73
00:05:37,880 --> 00:05:41,510
I heard they had 3 tall 
players in the 190 cm range,

74
00:05:41,510 --> 00:05:43,860
but it seems one of them 
is out with an injury.

75
00:05:44,540 --> 00:05:46,180
We were quite fortunate the freshman

76
00:05:46,180 --> 00:05:49,820
that they replaced him with is barely 
10 cm taller than Kurumatani.

77
00:05:50,080 --> 00:05:52,290
So one of their big guns
is down and out, huh?

78
00:05:52,290 --> 00:05:53,570
Talk about lucky!

79
00:05:53,570 --> 00:05:54,380
Totally!

80
00:05:54,380 --> 00:05:56,830
Don't celebrate the other 
team's injuries, you asswipes!

81
00:05:57,460 --> 00:05:59,230
But I do have to admit,

82
00:05:59,230 --> 00:06:02,750
dealing with 3 of those 190 cm titans 
would've been an absolute nightmare.

83
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:06,500
This is good, we just need
to keep scoring from outside the paint

84
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:08,710
and eventually they'll be forced 
to switch their defense.

85
00:06:09,460 --> 00:06:12,880
And then, if they start 
playing man-to-man instead,

86
00:06:12,960 --> 00:06:15,880
we can take advantage of matchups
against their #8 and #7.

87
00:06:15,960 --> 00:06:17,500
The guys Momoharu and I guard?

88
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:20,500
So that must mean the two 
of us are better than them.

89
00:06:20,500 --> 00:06:22,540
It's about time I got the spotlight!

90
00:06:22,710 --> 00:06:23,920
I'm gonna score all the baskets!

91
00:06:24,210 --> 00:06:25,500
That's not what I meant.

92
00:06:26,540 --> 00:06:30,290
If my guess is correct, those two
only started playing basketball in high school.

93
00:06:30,540 --> 00:06:31,580
Are you serious?!

94
00:06:31,830 --> 00:06:34,750
So then, like, they only have 
about a year of experience?

95
00:06:35,290 --> 00:06:37,920
That much is obvious just based
on how they move on the court.

96
00:06:38,330 --> 00:06:40,460
Although there's a slight 
gap in overall strength...

97
00:06:41,290 --> 00:06:44,210
...we can basically consider all of the things
that we struggled with up until now

98
00:06:44,380 --> 00:06:47,960
to also be the exact weaknesses
that our opponents suffer from.

99
00:06:49,380 --> 00:06:53,790
When going man-to-man in matches like this,
its the difference in individual skill that counts.

100
00:06:54,170 --> 00:06:56,410
To make up for that, their 
#4 and other players

101
00:06:56,410 --> 00:06:58,880
have been focused on providing 
the necessary backup.

102
00:06:59,250 --> 00:07:02,710
It's the exact same playstyle
that we've been practicing this whole time.

103
00:07:03,080 --> 00:07:06,500
When it comes to individual skills,
our team definitely has the advantage.

104
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:08,540
Let's drive them right into a corner!

105
00:07:09,290 --> 00:07:11,460
A'ight, boys! We're gonna trash 'em!

106
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:12,670
Yeah!

107
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:15,500
They've really changed.

108
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:18,040
They actually look like a 
normal basketball team now.

109
00:07:18,290 --> 00:07:22,710
Their team balance still needs some work,
but I'd say the odds favor Kuzu High at 60/40.

110
00:07:23,040 --> 00:07:24,170
You think so?

111
00:07:24,420 --> 00:07:26,210
I'd say they've actually 
got upwards of 70/30.

112
00:07:26,460 --> 00:07:29,210
You both know the world of 
basketball isn't that simple.

113
00:07:29,210 --> 00:07:30,340
Numbers don't mean squat.

114
00:07:33,460 --> 00:07:34,960
I finally remembered.

115
00:07:34,960 --> 00:07:35,460
Huh?

116
00:07:35,880 --> 00:07:38,830
Back in middle school,
there were twins on the team at Nakahara.

117
00:07:39,670 --> 00:07:41,580
That #7 out there was one of them.

118
00:07:42,170 --> 00:07:43,750
At Nakahara...?

119
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:49,130
Right, I forgot. You're not 
good with this kinda stuff.

120
00:07:50,500 --> 00:07:53,130
But I remember him really 
well, from that one game...

121
00:07:54,080 --> 00:07:57,290
He threw a bunch of incomplete passes
and then got benched at halftime for it.

122
00:07:57,960 --> 00:08:00,670
However, he wasn't really the problem.

123
00:08:01,170 --> 00:08:03,750
He was passing the ball about half a step
ahead of his teammates,

124
00:08:03,830 --> 00:08:06,750
but sadly none of them
could keep up with his excellent timing.

125
00:08:07,630 --> 00:08:11,170
Instead of waiting to pass when they got open,
his passes led them to being open.

126
00:08:11,670 --> 00:08:13,790
That's the ideal point guard 
you always talk about, yeah?

127
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:17,380
And that's exactly who we're competing
against right now.

128
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:21,710
The timing of his passes hasn't changed a bit,
in fact, they're even faster now.

129
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:28,210
Yanagihara, you're defending #15.

130
00:08:28,380 --> 00:08:31,080
It might be tough, but I need 
you to stick to him like glue.

131
00:08:31,080 --> 00:08:32,210
R-right!

132
00:08:32,210 --> 00:08:33,920
#11 is all yours, Roku.

133
00:08:33,920 --> 00:08:34,750
Got it.

134
00:08:35,170 --> 00:08:38,170
Thank you, Koji. I know 
just where to attack now.

135
00:08:40,130 --> 00:08:43,170
I'm gonna create our... 
window of opportunity.

136
00:08:45,380 --> 00:08:46,710
Smooth as silk, Roku!

137
00:08:46,920 --> 00:08:49,330
Don't embarrass me, dude!
Enough with the compliments!

138
00:08:49,540 --> 00:08:51,880
Seems this guy doesn't 
miss much from the middle.

139
00:08:52,040 --> 00:08:53,710
We should probably watch out 
for any threes from him.

140
00:08:53,710 --> 00:08:54,670
Defense!

141
00:09:06,250 --> 00:09:08,210
Shinjo suddenly changed up their defense!

142
00:09:08,420 --> 00:09:09,880
Man-to-man, huh?

143
00:09:10,080 --> 00:09:10,880
Perfect!

144
00:09:10,880 --> 00:09:12,720
Now we can start letting 
Natsume and Kurumatani

145
00:09:12,720 --> 00:09:14,720
drive our offense by 
going at them one-on-one.

146
00:09:16,130 --> 00:09:17,130
Hey, Nanao...

147
00:09:17,380 --> 00:09:18,710
...I'm worried about one thing.

148
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,130
I hate to say it, but...

149
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:25,620
Not everyone on our team wins
when it comes down to individual skill.

150
00:09:28,830 --> 00:09:46,960
Defense! Defense! Defense! Defense!

151
00:09:32,380 --> 00:09:34,580
Completely switching from zone was a mistake.

152
00:09:34,580 --> 00:09:37,290
They should've shutout the 
shrimp with a box and 1.

153
00:09:37,290 --> 00:09:38,670
I thought so, too.

154
00:09:38,670 --> 00:09:43,210
I highly doubt that #6 is gonna be able
to stop Kuzu High's #11 at all.

155
00:09:43,710 --> 00:09:46,960
I would've focused on defending inside the paint,
even if that weakened the outside.

156
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:52,250
You think it's gonna be easy
to take me one-on-one, then?

157
00:10:01,420 --> 00:10:03,130
Show him who's the boss, Chiaki!

158
00:10:09,630 --> 00:10:10,290
All right!

159
00:10:10,920 --> 00:10:11,750
Captain...

160
00:10:11,750 --> 00:10:14,170
Don't sweat it. He just took the bait.

161
00:10:15,290 --> 00:10:16,540
Roku, let me fill you in.

162
00:10:18,750 --> 00:10:21,960
While you're defending #11,
keep your eyes entirely on him.

163
00:10:25,880 --> 00:10:28,630
Nao was right... this guy isn't 
all that good at basketball.

164
00:10:30,960 --> 00:10:32,750
I might actually be better than he is!

165
00:10:33,380 --> 00:10:34,750
Quit shooting your mouth off!

166
00:10:40,750 --> 00:10:42,790
Gotta stick to him like glue! 
Gotta get up in his face!

167
00:10:47,580 --> 00:10:48,330
He's way too quick!

168
00:10:51,670 --> 00:10:52,880
Too close for comfort!

169
00:10:52,880 --> 00:10:54,960
You gotta do better, Yanagihara!

170
00:10:56,790 --> 00:10:58,540
That had to catch them by surprise.

171
00:10:58,540 --> 00:11:01,630
Even without scoring, his shots
definitely throw the defense off their game.

172
00:11:02,500 --> 00:11:04,920
Looks like the momentum isn't 
gonna shift anytime soon.

173
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:36,000
An interception!

174
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:37,000
Oh no, Chiaki's pass!

175
00:11:37,210 --> 00:11:38,210
Goddammit.

176
00:11:38,330 --> 00:11:40,460
Nice work, Yukio! Keep it up!

177
00:11:41,540 --> 00:11:44,920
Not again! The ball isn't getting passed around to me
when I stay in one place!

178
00:11:45,380 --> 00:11:47,880
But this guy's defense is making it hard for me
to cut in anywhere!

179
00:11:48,580 --> 00:11:52,170
He's constantly just watching my eyes
and hardly ever pays attention to the ball!

180
00:11:53,040 --> 00:11:56,170
This is exactly the time when we need
those crazy passes of yours!

181
00:11:56,830 --> 00:11:58,460
What exactly is the problem, bro?!

182
00:12:08,500 --> 00:12:10,920
Ugh, he got shutdown again.

183
00:12:11,330 --> 00:12:13,250
Kuzu High really isn't good 
at making fast breaks.

184
00:12:13,630 --> 00:12:15,380
Even though they're so fundamental.

185
00:12:15,500 --> 00:12:18,750
Nah, Shinjo's response time 
on defense is just that good.

186
00:12:18,750 --> 00:12:21,960
Although, I imagine that's because
they would lose quick otherwise.

187
00:12:22,250 --> 00:12:26,670
On the other hand, Kuzu High hasn't been able
to score any points recently...

188
00:12:26,750 --> 00:12:28,630
...except on those shitty fast breaks.

189
00:12:32,080 --> 00:12:33,330
He's driving to the basket!

190
00:12:41,670 --> 00:12:44,250
There are no openings for 
me... to pass through!

191
00:12:45,080 --> 00:12:46,080
They stopped him!

192
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:49,130
Kuzuryu ball!

193
00:12:49,710 --> 00:12:51,880
What is going on with Chiaki right now?

194
00:12:54,380 --> 00:12:57,670
Hey, Yasuhara! You gotta force your way inside
or you'll never get a pass!

195
00:12:58,000 --> 00:12:59,750
Did you forget what I 
taught you about cutting?

196
00:12:59,960 --> 00:13:01,000
O-okay!

197
00:13:03,500 --> 00:13:05,960
Have you noticed it, Tokiwa?

198
00:13:06,290 --> 00:13:07,130
Of course.

199
00:13:07,670 --> 00:13:10,630
Though it's hard to see
because of how subtle their movements are.

200
00:13:11,380 --> 00:13:13,280
By arranging their defense 
to focus on one side,

201
00:13:13,280 --> 00:13:16,150
they cut the space the point 
guard can work with in half.

202
00:13:16,500 --> 00:13:18,100
This traps the ball-handler, since the

203
00:13:18,100 --> 00:13:20,570
direction they can drive in 
and the direction they can

204
00:13:20,570 --> 00:13:22,480
pass to are both limited as a result.

205
00:13:23,250 --> 00:13:26,420
If the defenders in the open space
focus on closing any pass windows,

206
00:13:26,420 --> 00:13:28,670
the only thing the ball-handler
can do is go for the basket himself.

207
00:13:29,670 --> 00:13:32,450
The smartest thing they did 
was assuring the dead side of

208
00:13:32,450 --> 00:13:34,120
the court is the one that #11 is on.

209
00:13:34,420 --> 00:13:35,960
It's an extreme move that only

210
00:13:35,960 --> 00:13:39,590
works because Takahashi
trusts #6 to provide a solid enough defense.

211
00:13:40,830 --> 00:13:43,710
Letting #7 get free for that first basket
was also a good call.

212
00:13:44,130 --> 00:13:47,250
Thanks to that, he basically dropped his guard
and didn't notice what happened.

213
00:13:47,670 --> 00:13:49,210
Takahashi's really incredible.

214
00:13:49,790 --> 00:13:52,700
He's definitely not the type of guy
that'll go down quietly in the prelims.

215
00:13:52,700 --> 00:13:53,720
That's for sure.

216
00:13:55,670 --> 00:13:56,630
A steal!

217
00:14:00,880 --> 00:14:02,000
He's totally alone!

218
00:14:11,330 --> 00:14:12,880
The tide is turning!

219
00:14:13,250 --> 00:14:15,080
You're really fast on your feet.

220
00:14:16,210 --> 00:14:18,420
I didn't think anybody would catch up to me.

221
00:14:19,130 --> 00:14:22,210
Even though I caught up... I 
couldn't do a single thing!

222
00:14:23,580 --> 00:14:25,580
The problem isn't with Afro-senpai.

223
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:27,880
It's the fact that #4 is just too good.

224
00:14:28,920 --> 00:14:32,710
A big gap in skill between point guards...
can prove fatal in the end.

225
00:14:34,960 --> 00:14:37,210
Excuse me! We'd like a timeout...

226
00:14:38,580 --> 00:14:39,580
It was a bad pass!

227
00:14:39,580 --> 00:14:41,420
What's going on with Chiaki?!

228
00:14:41,540 --> 00:14:44,290
Why the hell do you think we spent
so long practicing screens?!

229
00:14:44,790 --> 00:14:46,250
You gotta keep it together and lead us!

230
00:14:46,250 --> 00:14:47,130
I know that!

231
00:14:47,630 --> 00:14:49,710
Looks like they're having 
trouble getting coordinated.

232
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:52,830
This is when the difference in teamwork
starts to really show.

233
00:14:56,420 --> 00:14:57,960
Time to do your stuff, Momoharu!

234
00:14:58,080 --> 00:14:59,460
I'm all over it!

235
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:06,670
Oh shit! I can't believe I 
fell for something so simple!

236
00:15:06,880 --> 00:15:08,750
Nice move, Tamo!

237
00:15:09,330 --> 00:15:10,830
Leave this one to me!

238
00:15:13,420 --> 00:15:14,540
What was that Tamo?!

239
00:15:14,540 --> 00:15:15,880
Keep it together!

240
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:19,250
Well then, this big oaf isn't so good
at sinking his shots, eh?

241
00:15:19,250 --> 00:15:21,170
I guess that makes us birds of a feather!

242
00:15:21,580 --> 00:15:22,830
Rebound!

243
00:15:28,540 --> 00:15:30,250
H-he came from above me?!

244
00:15:30,580 --> 00:15:31,670
That was wicked cool!

245
00:15:31,670 --> 00:15:33,210
You're the best, Takahashi!

246
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:37,130
Offensive foul! Charging! No count!

247
00:15:37,130 --> 00:15:38,130
So close!

248
00:15:38,880 --> 00:15:40,710
Obviously that wasn't gonna count.

249
00:15:40,710 --> 00:15:42,580
He just used him like a stepladder.

250
00:15:42,830 --> 00:15:46,130
That had to be a flagrant 
foul just now. No doubt.

251
00:15:46,330 --> 00:15:48,580
It did keep the momentum 
in their favor, though.

252
00:15:49,460 --> 00:15:51,710
This is gonna be a major pain in their ass.

253
00:15:52,420 --> 00:15:54,920
So, Kuzu High... how are you gonna react?

254
00:15:56,170 --> 00:15:57,380
Are you taking a timeout?

255
00:15:57,380 --> 00:16:00,580
Oh! Uh... Ummm...

256
00:16:02,580 --> 00:16:03,880
Get the lead out!

257
00:16:04,250 --> 00:16:06,170
Hey, Chiaki! Let's change up our positions.

258
00:16:06,630 --> 00:16:08,540
That will help us throw off 
the other team's rhythm.

259
00:16:08,830 --> 00:16:11,500
Forget it! I want you to focus
on pushing your way into the middle!

260
00:16:11,790 --> 00:16:15,000
Take advantage of screens from Momoharu.
Keep your eye out for the signs!

261
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:20,830
Never mind, it's nothing. I'm sorry.

262
00:16:21,630 --> 00:16:23,380
She changed her mind on the timeout.

263
00:16:24,500 --> 00:16:27,330
Are they seriously just gonna truck it through
the remaining 2 minutes?!

264
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:30,500
It's true that the momentum of the game
is shifting in our favor.

265
00:16:30,790 --> 00:16:33,540
But we've been pushing ourselves to play
at a higher pace than usual from the get-go.

266
00:16:33,710 --> 00:16:36,290
Our team isn't one that specializes 
in making fast breaks.

267
00:16:36,750 --> 00:16:40,210
So if they took a timeout, it would actually
take some of the strain off us, but...

268
00:16:41,080 --> 00:16:43,920
I can't imagine that she's actually reading
that deep into it.

269
00:16:50,130 --> 00:16:50,960
It's a fast break!

270
00:16:54,920 --> 00:16:56,080
He got open!

271
00:16:57,420 --> 00:16:59,330
Stop right there, dammit!

272
00:17:00,630 --> 00:17:02,790
No way I'm just gonna let you drop it in!

273
00:17:03,210 --> 00:17:03,830
Hiyah!

274
00:17:06,040 --> 00:17:08,830
A karate chop? No, I must be seeing things...

275
00:17:09,170 --> 00:17:11,170
Man, that pompadour guy can hustle!

276
00:17:11,170 --> 00:17:13,460
He caught up from way back 
there and stopped the shot!

277
00:17:13,460 --> 00:17:15,420
Yeah, but with a blatant foul.

278
00:17:15,630 --> 00:17:16,540
That hurts!

279
00:17:16,830 --> 00:17:19,750
Sorry 'bout that, man. 
It's a bad habit of mine.

280
00:17:20,920 --> 00:17:22,460
I'll shank you, asshole.

281
00:17:23,710 --> 00:17:26,000
Huh?! Try saying that again, bitch.

282
00:17:27,630 --> 00:17:28,880
Two free-throws!

283
00:17:38,960 --> 00:17:41,960
Tch. Start doing your job 
under the basket, dammit.

284
00:17:41,960 --> 00:17:43,380
Uh, right, I'm sorry.

285
00:17:43,380 --> 00:17:45,130
You have no room to talk, dude!

286
00:17:47,290 --> 00:17:49,500
That foul was a nice move. Props, Yasuhara.

287
00:17:49,500 --> 00:17:52,540
Thanks to that, we managed
to knock some of the wind out of their sails!

288
00:17:53,580 --> 00:17:55,710
Never thought I'd get praised for fouling!

289
00:17:56,290 --> 00:17:58,130
A'ight! Let's keep them on their toes!

290
00:17:58,130 --> 00:18:00,630
Can do! Just leave everything to me!

291
00:18:01,540 --> 00:18:02,210
Dammit!

292
00:18:12,460 --> 00:18:13,330
Switch!

293
00:18:16,080 --> 00:18:16,880
Amazing!

294
00:18:25,670 --> 00:18:27,130
Whoa, what a pass!

295
00:18:32,540 --> 00:18:33,380
Uh oh...

296
00:18:33,380 --> 00:18:34,960
There was nobody there...

297
00:18:35,460 --> 00:18:36,500
Shinjo ball!

298
00:18:36,500 --> 00:18:38,460
Seriously? Is that guy an amateur or what?

299
00:18:40,580 --> 00:18:41,500
Now I'm pissed!

300
00:18:41,710 --> 00:18:43,500
That was some very precise passing.

301
00:18:43,920 --> 00:18:45,130
You almost got us.

302
00:18:46,960 --> 00:18:49,580
But unfortunately this little 
guy didn't get in the clear.

303
00:18:49,830 --> 00:18:53,250
With everybody clustered in the middle,
it opened up a weak side.

304
00:18:53,540 --> 00:18:57,080
Takahashi and that shorty both foresaw
a pass coming that direction.

305
00:18:57,630 --> 00:19:01,290
But Takahashi expertly stopped
their #15 from getting there.

306
00:19:03,540 --> 00:19:05,830
Recognizing our opponent's 
skills is the first step.

307
00:19:06,380 --> 00:19:07,750
The real game starts after that.

308
00:19:08,250 --> 00:19:10,250
The members of that team all have good sense.

309
00:19:10,670 --> 00:19:12,370
Both passer and receiver know where the ball

310
00:19:12,370 --> 00:19:14,170
needs to move for them to score points.

311
00:19:14,500 --> 00:19:17,750
Unfortunately, that's just not 
a skill that our team has.

312
00:19:17,920 --> 00:19:18,920
Captain...

313
00:19:19,290 --> 00:19:21,920
However, we can still win this.

314
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:26,040
Geniuses are actually... 
surprisingly fragile.

315
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:31,330
Taking a timeout would be best...

316
00:19:31,630 --> 00:19:34,080
I think this is an instance 
where we need to gamble.

317
00:19:34,920 --> 00:19:36,540
It's true that we're being 
pushed into a corner,

318
00:19:36,750 --> 00:19:39,500
but it looks to me like Shinjo's players
are pushing themselves to move quickly.

319
00:19:40,830 --> 00:19:42,410
If we let them take a breather now,

320
00:19:42,410 --> 00:19:45,530
it might backfire and build 
up their momentum even more.

321
00:19:47,580 --> 00:19:49,000
But just look at what's 
happening in the meantime!

322
00:19:49,290 --> 00:19:51,000
Not happening, Sideburns!

323
00:19:55,460 --> 00:19:56,380
All right!

324
00:19:56,380 --> 00:19:58,290
We're on fire right now!

325
00:19:58,670 --> 00:20:00,170
Just one minute left.

326
00:20:00,170 --> 00:20:02,540
It'll hurt if Shinjo makes a comeback
just before this quarter ends.

327
00:20:02,540 --> 00:20:05,830
Especially considering Kuzu High 
had the advantage for most of it.

328
00:20:05,830 --> 00:20:07,220
It'll definitely bring their spirits down.

329
00:20:07,750 --> 00:20:09,130
More importantly, Chiba...

330
00:20:09,670 --> 00:20:11,960
Have you noticed something 
strange with Shinjo's #7?

331
00:20:12,540 --> 00:20:15,060
His defense and shooting 
ability are lackluster,

332
00:20:15,060 --> 00:20:18,120
but his drives are really 
clean and effective.

333
00:20:18,710 --> 00:20:21,670
Aside from that earlier foul,
he hasn't missed a single layup.

334
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:23,400
Now that you mention it,

335
00:20:23,400 --> 00:20:27,120
he does have a playstyle
that seems vaguely similar to Takahashi's.

336
00:20:29,380 --> 00:20:30,580
I let him slip by! Damn!

337
00:20:37,080 --> 00:20:38,380
His pass timing is way off!

338
00:20:38,380 --> 00:20:39,580
What's wrong with you, Chiaki?!

339
00:20:42,750 --> 00:20:43,880
That was nuts!

340
00:20:43,880 --> 00:20:45,500
I can't believe he made that work!

341
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:47,210
This is really throwing me off my game!

342
00:20:52,710 --> 00:20:53,920
He couldn't get it all the way in!

343
00:20:56,290 --> 00:20:57,210
It's gonna come back down!

344
00:20:57,210 --> 00:20:58,170
Box them out!

345
00:20:59,920 --> 00:21:01,250
Chiaki's in trouble!

346
00:21:01,250 --> 00:21:03,670
Am I crazy or is this just 
getting worse and worse for us?!

347
00:21:04,250 --> 00:21:05,800
The worst part is that

348
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:07,990
Chiaki has been thrown off
both offensively and defensively,

349
00:21:07,990 --> 00:21:10,120
which affects the rhythm of the entire team!

350
00:21:10,580 --> 00:21:12,630
We need this basket... no matter what!

351
00:21:12,960 --> 00:21:14,290
Rebound!

352
00:21:21,040 --> 00:21:22,630
Gotta be gentle, just a light tap!

353
00:21:22,960 --> 00:21:25,580
We need to score here or 
else we're in real trouble!

354
00:21:32,750 --> 00:21:35,580
He tipped it in!

355
00:21:36,710 --> 00:21:39,580
I think that's the first time
I've ever seen him score a basket.

356
00:21:39,580 --> 00:21:41,290
How does a guy like that end up as center?

357
00:21:41,960 --> 00:21:44,600
Well, with this basket and 
the earlier foul from #5,

358
00:21:44,600 --> 00:21:47,240
I think they put a stop to Shinjo's run.

359
00:21:47,710 --> 00:21:50,170
What's the deal, Chiaki? 
This ain't like you, man.

360
00:21:50,170 --> 00:21:51,040
Huh?

361
00:21:51,750 --> 00:21:54,500
Do you wanna go watch this game
from the bench, or what?!

362
00:21:55,630 --> 00:21:58,460
Easy for you to say, pea-brain.

363
00:23:31,040 --> 00:23:35,420
Ahiru no Sora

364
00:23:31,710 --> 00:23:34,000
Next episode: "The Hard Play."

